From 21cb01dd37b94e26f5739969c98c72091f0331a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 02:47:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/36] MessageView: include Common/MetaTypes.h for
 QList<QByteArray> metatype

message.data(...).value<QList<QByteArray>>() needs the
Q_DECLARE_METATYPE(QList<QByteArray>) specialization from
Common/MetaTypes.h visible in this translation unit -- Qt5
auto-derives container metatypes so this compiled without the
include there, but Qt4 requires the explicit declaration to be
visible wherever the type crosses QVariant. Not an automoc issue (the
error surfaces compiling MessageView.cpp directly, not moc-generated
code); confirmed CMAKE_AUTOMOC is unchanged from v0.6, the last
release that genuinely built on Qt4, so it isn't the culprit here.

Swept every other file using a type declared via Q_DECLARE_METATYPE
elsewhere in the tree (Message::Envelope, ThreadingNode, ImapTask*,
ConnectionMethod, CacheLoadingMode, SignatureDataBundle,
QMap<QByteArray,QByteArray>) against a full transitive-include
resolution (not just direct/one-hop, since several are only reachable
via MailboxTree.h -> Parser/Message.h) -- no further gaps found.
---
 src/Gui/MessageView.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/Gui/MessageView.cpp b/src/Gui/MessageView.cpp
index 26c3b68d..2fa0b91d 100644
--- a/src/Gui/MessageView.cpp
+++ b/src/Gui/MessageView.cpp
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@
 #include <QStackedLayout>
 
 #include "Common/InvokeMethod.h"
+#include "Common/MetaTypes.h"
 #include "Common/SettingsNames.h"
 #include "Composer/QuoteText.h"
 #include "Composer/SubjectMangling.h"
